  "term": "virtual reality therapy",
  "definition": "Virtual reality therapy is a treatment method that places a person in an immersive, interactive computer-generated three-dimensional setting. The virtual environment is used to increase a sense of presence, reduce avoidance, and support emotional engagement.",
